  id: Levator_labii_superioris_muscle.L
  partName: Levator labii superioris muscle L
  descriptionChunks:
  - The levator labii superioris raises the upper lip, exposing the upper teeth and
    contributing to expressions such as smiling, snarling, or showing displeasure.
    It plays an important role in speech articulation by adjusting the position of
    the lip. This muscle works in coordination with other facial muscles to produce
    complex expressions and movements.
  - ' It is also involved in emotional signaling, helping convey reactions like disgust,
    aggression, or surprise through controlled elevation of the upper lip.'
